A||||3||jmw||How many on the road?||||7||
Z||000000||jmw||09-14-2000||08:10 PM||||If you had to guess, how many Fieros would you say are still on the road [by year and country]? Just curious, as mine is one of something like 140,000 supposedly built in '84. I sure don't see many around where I live.<P>Sorry - don't know why this double-posted!<p>[This message has been edited by jmw (edited 09-14-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||fiero56||09-14-2000||08:14 PM||||I was just asking myself that question yesterday. I would assume that about half of all Fieros produced, are still on the roads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||09-15-2000||01:32 AM||||I asked that question with the topic "Show me the numbers".  This week I email'd Pontiac and asked them.  The response was "don't know".  Sheesh.  Guess it's up to us to think of a way to be as accurate as possible.  Best thing I've seen yet is John Wilhoff's 88 database... <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/database.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487/database.html</A> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||88 Database Guy||09-15-2000||07:53 AM||||Hi Guys, <P>Thanks Cheever2, this is indeed one of the questions that I'm trying to get a handle on with this project.  I'm really pressed for time this AM, but from the numbers so far, some interesting trends are developing. The numbers of cars of each color and model in the database allow me to calculate the percentage of Reds, Blacks, etc that I'm getting info on. As we get more and more cars, the percentages of cars of a specific color are getting very close to the percentages of the number built.  In other words, the numbers in the database tell me that we're seeing a fairly complete representation of the '88s built, and it's not skewed towards any one color.  The model<BR>percentages are not so close, mainly because alot of the info is coming from GT and Formula owners, rather than coupe owners, and because I suspect many more coupes have met their end already.  I recently got some fantastic input from a friend who gave me the entire headcount of a certain state's Fieros!  Don't ask me for details, but as soon as I can get some time to check the population count for this state, and come up with a ratio vs the whole country, that ought<BR>to give us a fair number (+/- 10%?) of the total that are still out there.<P>Stay tuned for more, thanks for everybody's help.<P>John Willhoff john.willhoff@gulfaero.com (770) 578-6556 (912) 898-1389||||reg||10
